ot the\nfull argv and not the resolved binary path. So a pattern like ",[201,1212,1213],{},"npx-mytool*"," from an\nearlier revision could never match a server launched as ",[201,1216,1217],{},"[\"npx\", \"my-mcp-tool\"]",";\nuse ",[201,1220,1221],{},"npx*",", or disambiguate with an absolute executable path (",[201,1224,1225],{},"\u002Fusr\u002Flocal\u002Fbin\u002Fmytool",")\nand pin that. An exact ",[201,1228,403],{}," cannot discriminate between two servers launched\nyou the same executable — thin per-server sandboxing must live server-side.",[141,1231,1232],{},"The allowlist lives at the daemon\u002Fembedding boundary — the operator decides which MCP\nservers the scheduler may call, not the tasks.json author.",[141,1234,1235,1236,1239,1240,1243,1244,1247,1248,1251],{},"An http server-only spec must carry a tool dimension (",[201,1237,1238],{},"url:*"," or ",[201,1241,1242],{},"url:tool","); a\nbare ",[201,1245,1246],{},"https:\u002F\u002Fhost"," fails at load — it would parse as server ",[201,1249,1250],{},"https"," and silently\nmatch nothing (a footgun on a security allowlist).",[1253,1254,1255],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .soVBu, html code.shiki .soVBu{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#999999;--shiki-dark:#666666}html pre.shiki code .s4Jsk, html code.shiki .s4Jsk{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#99841877;--shiki-dark:#B8A96577}html pre.shiki code .sLorS, html code.shiki .sLorS{--shiki-light:#9C3EDA;--shiki-default:#998418;--shiki-dark:#B8A965}html pre.shiki code .sa2tF, html code.shiki .sa2tF{--shiki-light:#E2931D;--shiki-default:#998418;--shiki-dark:#B8A965}html pre.shiki code .sbYkP, html code.shiki .sbYkP{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#B5695977;--shiki-dark:#C98A7D77}html pre.shiki code .sTbE_, html code.shiki .sTbE_{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#B56959;--shiki-dark:#C98A7D}html pre.shiki code .skNjk, html code.shiki .skNjk{--shiki-light:#F76D47;--shiki-default:#998418;--shiki-dark:#B8A965}html pre.shiki code .suXOh, html co